operating-system-1
==================

A Linux-based operating-system project working toward a cohesive,
macOS-inspired desktop experience with original system applications and assets.
This is not macOS, is not affiliated with Apple, and does not provide macOS
binary compatibility.

Current development stage: Phase 1 -- kernel-to-shell foundation VERIFIED
on reference commit 4cc3727310198a1df85f47a818873477bcd31f5b.
Two clean GitHub Actions attempts passed the full kernel/BusyBox build and four
QEMU boot scenarios; the acceptance record and downloadable evidence are in
docs/os/PHASE_01.md. Each newer commit must pass its own CI validation.
Phase 2 has not begun. There is no desktop, installer, live ISO, or bare-metal
support claim yet.

Quick start (Linux x86-64)
-------------------------

Install the host prerequisites listed in docs/os/PHASE_01.md, then run from
the repository root:

    make -C distro/phase1 check
    make -C distro/phase1 build
    make -C distro/phase1 test
    make -C distro/phase1 run

The build uses this repository's kernel and a pinned, statically linked
BusyBox userspace. The automated tests boot in QEMU software emulation (TCG),
so they do not require KVM, a privileged VM runner, or access to host disks.
All build output and disposable virtual storage remain in .build/phase1/.

The test suite covers two boots with ext4 persistence, DHCP networking, an
actual interactive serial shell session, clean poweroff, and a deliberately
broken initramfs. A successful QEMU exit alone is not considered a pass.

Documentation
-------------

    docs/os/PHASE_01.md              Scope, commands, acceptance criteria
    docs/os/BUILD_PROVENANCE.md      Source/dependency pins and evidence
    docs/os/BOOT_TROUBLESHOOTING.md  Build and boot failure diagnosis

GitHub Actions: https://github.com/boop-bip80/operating-system-1/actions
Each Phase 1 run publishes its available build and test evidence as an
artifact, including failed runs. Artifacts have a 14-day retention period;
download evidence needed for a lasting release/review record.

Kernel provenance and licensing
-------------------------------

This repository retains the Linux kernel source tree. The Phase 1 starting
point is commit 1c542b368c25323551c74278e64a886ed0c6f129 on rcu-free-v3;
its Makefile identifies Linux 7.3-rc7. New builds record the exact source
commit actually built rather than treating this historical baseline as HEAD.
The release-candidate kernel and virtual-machine test coverage are not a
production stability or hardware-qualification guarantee.

The distro scaffolding is isolated in distro/phase1/, and generated files
are kept out of the kernel source directories. The root kernel Makefile is
unchanged by the Phase 1 orchestration.

See COPYING, LICENSES/, and Documentation/process/license-rules.rst for the
Linux kernel's GPL-2.0 terms, syscall exception, and per-file licensing.
BusyBox and the static C library retain their own license obligations;
source versions, checksums, and redistribution notes are recorded in
docs/os/BUILD_PROVENANCE.md. Preserve these notices when redistributing.

Upstream kernel documentation: https://docs.kernel.org/
Kernel build instructions: Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst
